sec.p:
At the stage of “valuation,” the decision-maker forms the expected values for the 2 choices (Qlarge and Qsmall) by multiplying the class probabilities by the learned values of the corresponding choices (Vlarge and Vsmall) as follows:




Qlarge=p(CL=large)×Vlarge;







Qsmall=p(CL=small)×Vsmall.
